  "notes": "TDE's in-house crew, and what separates them from the label's later work is stated plainly: \"drier and more sample-forward than the label's later, glossier work.\" The distinguishing parameters are the key centre and the residue. The research names **flat keys — D♭, F, B♭ minor** — so `session.keys` is authored (C#m/Fm/A#m/Gm) rather than inherited, which is the one hard fact this entry has that the lane does not. \"Sample-derived 7th/9th residue\" puts 55% of `extensions` above the triad even though the harmony is `i–VI–III–VII` and static-minor beds, and \"harmonic motion inherited from the sample\" is why `chordDurationBeats` runs to 16 — the loop, not the writer, decides when a chord changes. \"Small human offsets\" on the MPC-lineage kit is `quantizeStrength` 0.78 with `snare.offGridMs` 4 and a clap offset of 3-9ms. ⚠ `medium`, and the research says why: the collective's role, lineage and archive workflow are documented but \"individual members' drum signatures not separately sourced [LOW-CONF]\". The INFERRED parameters are every drum number below — kick anchors, ghost placement, hat density — which are the lane's MPC grammar rather than a Tae Beast or Willie B reading. ⚠ The crew's documented archive practice (\"97,000 gigs of beats\", placements chosen years later) is a workflow fact with no MIDI-facing parameter, so it is recorded here and modeled nowhere. ⚠ The 130–140 half-time population is not modeled: `halfTime` is one boolean and this entry authors no modes.",
